--- Inside a function `grad` differentiates, a list of lists holds traced
--- tensors as a list does, and a record holding them shows as the record
--- does, its numbers read off the tape. Compiled, a list of lists of them
--- had not built (the traced form went one list deep), and neither had
--- `log` of the record (its traced twin showed nothing), where the
--- interpreter ran both. By hand: d/dx (Σ 2x + Σ x²) = 2 + 2x.
use math
struct State [h, c]

fn grid[x]
    rows = []
    for i in range[2]
        rows = push[rows, push[push[[], x .* 2.0], x .* x]]
    return sum[rows[1][0]] + sum[rows[0][1]]

fn shown[x]
    s = State[x .* 2.0, x .* x]
    log[s]
    log[s.h]
    return sum[s.h] + sum[s.c]

x = tensor[[1.0, 2.0]]
log[grad[grid][x]]
log[grad[shown][x]]
